{"type": "text", "timestamp": 1790923273655, "sessionID": "ses_f04a9969cffezb6G14uH3m50cJ", "part": {"id": "prt_0fb584758001oMb6X45y5m2eGE_text-0", "sessionID": "ses_f04a9969cffezb6G14uH3m50cJ", "messageID": "msg_0fb584758001oMb6X45y5m2eGE", "type": "text", "text": "The web search was cancelled, but the pixel analysis is conclusive enough on its own.\n\n**What the barcode shows:**\n\n- **Palette:** 98 of 1000 stripes lean blue-gray, the rest are muted khaki/olive/brown. There are **zero reddish stripes and zero green stripes** \u2014 saturation is uniformly low (mostly \u22640.2).\n- **Brightness:** everything is dim; the brightest block peaks at ~L=113 (no white or bright pastel regions), with a very dark stretch at ~85\u201391% (near-black at 90\u201391%), a lone steel-blue stripe inside that darkness (~88%), and a dark reddish-brown final stripe.\n\n**How that eliminates the candidates:**\n\n- **Zulu (H)** \u2014 bright veldt skies and red coats \u2192 no red anywhere.\n- **Capricorn One (I)** \u2014 the Mars-set sequence guarantees long red stripes \u2192 none.\n- **Aguirre (J)** \u2014 green jungle + blue river \u2192 zero green stripes.\n- **Assault on Precinct 13 (E)** \u2014 dark, but amber interiors and red fire/blood \u2192 zero warm stripes.\n- **Day of the Dead (D)** \u2014 fluorescent-white lab interiors and a blood-red finale \u2192 brightest stripe here is only L\u2248113 and no red.\n- **Nosferatu (A)** \u2014 candle/lantern amber throughout \u2192 barcode is cool, not warm.\n- **The Importance of Being Earnest (C)** / **Little Boy (F)** \u2014 bright pastel/sunny palettes \u2192 too bright.\n- **The Haunting in Connecticut (B)** \u2014 desaturated teal is plausible, but the film's digital look and brighter whites don't match the deep true blacks and khaki military tones.\n\n**Best match:** a muted WWII-era film with khaki/olive uniforms, steel-blue sea/sky/night scenes, bright daytime field/coastal stretches mid-film (the peaks at 20\u201323%, 37\u201339%, 44\u201347%), and a long very-dark night battle finale (85\u201391%) \u2014 the classic profile of **The Eagle Has Landed (1976)**: Eastern-front coastal blues early, Norfolk countryside khaki in the middle, and the night-time village firefight near the end.\n\nAnswer: G", "time": {"start": 1790923261790, "end": 1790923273655}}}
